Meticulous — very careful and precise
Example: She is meticulous about her work details.


Resilient — able to recover quickly from difficulties
Example: Children are often very resilient after setbacks.


Abundant — existing in large quantities
Example: Fresh mangoes are abundant in summer.


Ambiguous — unclear or having more than one meaning
Example: His answer was ambiguous and confusing.


Innovative — introducing new ideas or methods
Example: The company launched an innovative app.


Reluctant — unwilling or hesitant
Example: He was reluctant to speak in public.


Diligent — hardworking and careful
Example: She is a diligent student.


Fragile — easily broken or damaged
Example: The glass vase is very fragile.


Enhance — to improve or increase quality
Example: Exercise can enhance your mood.


Versatile — able to do many different things well
Example: A smartphone is a versatile device.


